Looking at this more carefully, the most likely root cause across all attempts producing identical "0 tasks created" results is a mismatch in class/method visibility when overriding `npsp.TDTM_Runnable.run()`, which is declared `global virtual` in the managed package. NPSP's own documented custom TDTM handler examples consistently use `global class ... global override ...`. I'm aligning with that exact pattern, performing the insert directly (so behavior doesn't depend on a dispatcher further processing the `DmlWrapper`), and using an `Id`-keyed map instead of positional indexing into `oldlist` for safer, more robust transition detection.

